description:
The image shows a list of five points in white text on a black background, providing advice for writers on how characters in a novel should speak. Each point begins with a number in parentheses. The points are as follows:

(1) telling us something about themselves;
(2) conveying information that may well advance the storyline and/or plot;
(3) adding to the music or the mood of the scene, story, or novel;
(4) giving us a scene from a different POV (especially if the character who is speaking is not connected directly to the narrative voice); and/or
(5) giving the novel a pedestrian feel.

At the bottom of the image, the quote is attributed to "Jane Smiley, via Walter Mosley" and the source is mentioned as "TheUnNovelist.com". The overall theme of the image is to provide guidance on effective dialogue writing in novels.
